# HTTP JSON envelope (`src/shared/http`)

## Responses

- Build responses with **`apiSuccessResponse`** and **`apiErrorResponse`** from [`apiResponse.ts`](src/shared/http/apiResponse.ts).
- Success body shape: `{ status, message, data }` where `status` mirrors the HTTP status code.
- Error body shape: `{ status, message, data, traceId }` — **every client-facing error** must include **`traceId`** (from `getHttpApiTraceId`).
- Always set **`content-type: application/json`** via those helpers (do not hand-roll headers unless extending the helper).

## Parsing

- Use **`parseJsonBody`** / **`JsonObjectBodyValidation`** for request bodies; surface parse failures as **`apiErrorResponse`** with status **400** and the shared messages from that module.

When adding new response helpers, keep the same field names so clients and tests stay stable.
